<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Reapit → Inspect360 Integration Guide</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --ink: #1a2332;
      --muted: #5a6a7a;
      --line: #d8e0e8;
      --bg: #f4f7fa;
      --card: #ffffff;
      --accent: #0d6e6e;
      --accent-soft: #e6f4f4;
      --warn: #8a5a00;
      --warn-bg: #fff6e5;
      --ok: #1b6b3a;
      --ok-bg: #e8f6ee;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      color: var(--ink);
      background: var(--bg);
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
    .hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0d3d4d 0%, #0d6e6e 55%, #1a8f8f 100%);
      color: #fff;
      padding: 3rem 1.5rem 2.5rem;
    }
    .hero-inner, .wrap {
      max-width: 880px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
    .hero h1 {
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
      font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }
    .hero p {
      margin: 0;
      max-width: 42rem;
      opacity: 0.92;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }
    .badge-row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.5rem;
      margin-top: 1.25rem;
    }
    .badge {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 0.25rem 0.7rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.18);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.28);
    }
    nav.toc {
      background: var(--card);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem;
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      z-index: 10;
    }
    nav.toc .wrap {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
    nav.toc a {
      color: var(--accent);
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    nav.toc a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
    main.wrap { padding: 2rem 1.5rem 3.5rem; }
    section {
      background: var(--card);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
      box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(26, 35, 50, 0.04);
    }
    h2 {
      margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      color: var(--accent);
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }
    h3 {
      margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    p { margin: 0 0 0.85rem; color: var(--ink); }
    p:last-child, ul:last-child, ol:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    ul, ol { margin: 0 0 0.85rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
    li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
    .muted { color: var(--muted); }
    .flow {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.65rem;
      margin: 1rem 0;
    }
    .flow-step {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
      gap: 0.85rem;
      align-items: start;
      padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      border-radius: 10px;
    }
    .step-num {
      width: 1.75rem;
      height: 1.75rem;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #fff;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    .step-body strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.15rem; }
    .step-body span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; }
    .grid-2 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 0.85rem;
      margin: 1rem 0;
    }
    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .grid-2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
    .pill-card {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 1rem;
      background: #fafcfd;
    }
    .pill-card h3 { margin-top: 0; }
    .pill-card.ok { border-color: #b7dfc5; background: var(--ok-bg); }
    .pill-card.warn { border-color: #f0d9a0; background: var(--warn-bg); }
    .pill-card.ok h3 { color: var(--ok); }
    .pill-card.warn h3 { color: var(--warn); }
    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      font-size: 0.92rem;
      margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    }
    th, td {
      text-align: left;
      padding: 0.55rem 0.65rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    th {
      background: #eef3f7;
      font-weight: 650;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    code {
      font-family: ui-monospace, "Cascadia Code", Consolas, monospace;
      font-size: 0.86em;
      background: #eef2f6;
      padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .callout {
      border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
      border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
      margin: 1rem 0 0;
    }
    footer {
      text-align: center;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      padding: 0 1.5rem 2.5rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <h1>Reapit → Inspect360 Integration</h1>
      <p>
        A one-way sync that brings lettings properties, landlords, tenants, and tenancies
        from Reapit Foundations into Inspect360 — so your team can inspect, maintain, and
        stay compliant without re-typing the portfolio.
      </p>
      <div class="badge-row">
        <span class="badge">One-way: Reapit → Inspect360</span>
        <span class="badge">Per organisation</span>
        <span class="badge">OAuth + encrypted tokens</span>
        <span class="badge">Live webhooks</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="Contents">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a href="#how">How it works</a>
      <a href="#help">How it helps</a>
      <a href="#setup">What you need to do</a>
      <a href="#use">How to use it</a>
      <a href="#data">What gets synced</a>
      <a href="#limits">Limits (v1)</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <main class="wrap">
    <section id="how">
      <h2>How Reapit is integrated</h2>
      <p>
        Each Inspect360 organisation can connect its own Reapit agency account.
        After connect, Inspect360 stores the Reapit customer id and encrypted tokens on the server
        (never in the browser). A background worker then imports data and keeps it updated.
      </p>

      <div class="flow">
        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="step-num">1</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <strong>Connect (OAuth)</strong>
            <span>Owner clicks Connect in Settings → Integrations. Reapit authorises the app. Inspect360 saves the customer id and encrypted tokens, then queues an initial sync.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="step-num">2</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <strong>Full sync (job worker)</strong>
            <span>Jobs run in Postgres (no Redis). Order: lettings properties → landlords/contacts → tenancies. Each Reapit id is mapped to an Inspect360 row so re-sync is idempotent.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="step-num">3</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <strong>Ongoing updates (webhooks)</strong>
            <span>Reapit posts to <code>/api/webhooks/reapit</code>. Signatures are verified (Ed25519). Events are de-duplicated by <code>eventId</code>. The organisation is resolved from Reapit’s customer id — not from a client-supplied org header.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-step">
          <div class="step-num">4</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <strong>Ownership split</strong>
            <span>Reapit overwrites identity fields on mapped rows (name, address, landlord, tenant, lease dates, rent). Inspect360 keeps owning inspections, maintenance, compliance, assets, and disputes — those are never written back to Reapit in v1.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Landlord in Inspect360</strong> is a Contact with type <em>Landlord</em> — not a login user.
        Tenants become both a Contact and a tenant user (portal access off until you enable it).
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="help">
      <h2>How it helps us</h2>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="pill-card ok">
          <h3>Less double entry</h3>
          <p class="muted" style="margin:0">Properties, tenants, landlords, and tenancy dates flow from Reapit instead of being typed twice.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pill-card ok">
          <h3>Ready for operations</h3>
          <p class="muted" style="margin:0">Once synced, the portfolio is ready for inspections, maintenance, compliance, and rent tools inside Inspect360.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pill-card ok">
          <h3>Stays up to date</h3>
          <p class="muted" style="margin:0">Initial/manual sync plus webhooks keep changes from Reapit flowing in without daily CSV imports.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pill-card ok">
          <h3>Safe boundaries</h3>
          <p class="muted" style="margin:0">Tokens stay server-side. Org isolation is enforced. Disconnecting drops tokens but keeps Inspect360 history.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="setup">
      <h2>What needs to be done to use it</h2>
      <p class="muted">These steps are done once per environment (dev / production), then each agency owner connects their own Reapit account.</p>

      <h3>1. Reapit Developer Portal (external)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Register an Inspect360 app in the Reapit Developer Portal.</li>
        <li>Redirect URL: <code>{BASE_URL}/api/reapit/oauth/callback</code></li>
        <li>Webhook URL: <code>{BASE_URL}/api/webhooks/reapit</code></li>
        <li>Scopes: <code>properties.read</code>, <code>contacts.read</code>, <code>landlords.read</code>, <code>tenancies.read</code>, and <code>tenancies.write</code> (required by Reapit for tenancy webhook delivery — Inspect360 still does not write to Reapit).</li>
        <li>Have a sandbox / customer id available for testing (e.g. SBOX).</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2. Server environment variables</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Variable</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>REAPIT_CLIENT_ID</code></td><td>App client id from Reapit</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>REAPIT_CLIENT_SECRET</code></td><td>App client secret</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>REAPIT_CONNECT_URL</code></td><td>Default <code>https://connect.reapit.cloud</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>REAPIT_API_URL</code></td><td>Default <code>https://platform.reapit.cloud</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>REAPIT_REDIRECT_URI</code></td><td>Optional override for the OAuth callback</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>INTEGRATION_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code></td><td>32-byte hex key for token encryption + OAuth state (<code>openssl rand -hex 32</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>ENABLE_REAPIT_WORKER</code></td><td>Defaults on; set <code>false</code> to pause the job worker</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3>3. Database migration (Contabo)</h3>
      <p>
        Run <code>server/migrations/addReapitIntegration.sql</code> as database user <code>creativecloud</code>
        (not <code>inspect360</code>). The script creates Reapit tables, adds the <code>landlord</code> contact type,
        and grants access to the app user.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Dev: <code>docker exec -it postgres psql -U creativecloud -d inspect360_dev</code></li>
        <li>Prod: <code>docker exec -it postgres psql -U creativecloud -d inspect360</code></li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4. Redeploy / restart the app</h3>
      <p>So routes, worker, and env vars are live. Then proceed to “How to use it” below.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="use">
      <h2>How to use it day to day</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Owner</strong> opens <strong>Settings → Integrations</strong>.</li>
        <li>In the <strong>Reapit</strong> card, click <strong>Connect Reapit</strong> and complete Reapit login / consent.</li>
        <li>After redirect, an <strong>initial sync</strong> is queued automatically. Status, entity counts, and sync history appear on the same card.</li>
        <li>Use <strong>Sync now</strong> anytime for a full refresh (owner only).</li>
        <li>On a property detail page (owner/clerk), mapped properties show <strong>Source: Reapit</strong> and last synced time.</li>
        <li>Landlords appear under <strong>Contacts</strong> with type Landlord. Tenants appear as tenant users/assignments (portal off until you enable access).</li>
        <li><strong>Disconnect</strong> disables the link and drops tokens; Inspect360 property/tenant data remains.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="callout">
        Connect / disconnect / sync are <strong>owner</strong> actions. Clerks can view connection status and sync history.
        Trial / credit locks also apply to <code>/api/reapit</code> endpoints (except the public webhook path).
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="data">
      <h2>What gets synced</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>From Reapit</th><th>Into Inspect360</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Lettings properties</td>
            <td><code>properties</code></td>
            <td>Address formatted into one field. Sales-only stock skipped.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Landlords (+ related contact)</td>
            <td><code>contacts</code> type <strong>landlord</strong></td>
            <td>Not a login user. Optional link on the property via <code>landlordContactId</code>.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Tenant contacts</td>
            <td><code>contacts</code> + <code>users</code> (role tenant)</td>
            <td>Portal access starts off. Email collisions use a synthetic login email when needed.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Tenancies</td>
            <td><code>tenant_assignments</code></td>
            <td>Lease dates, rent, deposit. Ended tenancies set inactive. Rent periods generated.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="limits">
      <h2>What v1 does not do</h2>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="pill-card warn">
          <h3>No write-back</h3>
          <p class="muted" style="margin:0">Inspections, maintenance, and compliance stay in Inspect360 only.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pill-card warn">
          <h3>No document blitz</h3>
          <p class="muted" style="margin:0">Reapit document binaries and property image bulk import are out of scope for v1.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pill-card warn">
          <h3>No auto blocks</h3>
          <p class="muted" style="margin:0">Units sync as standalone properties unless you organise them later in Inspect360.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pill-card warn">
          <h3>No hard deletes</h3>
          <p class="muted" style="margin:0">Archived Reapit records are not deleted in Inspect360; we stop updating identity fields.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    Inspect360 · Reapit Foundations integration guide · open this file in any browser
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
